{
  "summary": "This experiment tested weighted fusion in a multimodal setup using PCA-encoded RNA and ResNet50-encoded images, achieving validation accuracy of 0.5232 and F1 of 0.5084, slightly lower than the concatenation baseline (llm_summary_001) but within a narrow range. The results suggest weighted fusion may not outperform concatenation in this configuration, though uncertainty remains about the relative effectiveness of fusion strategies without direct comparison to other methods. The multimodal foundation's superiority over RNA-only models (llm_summary_002) is confirmed, but fusion design choices require further exploration."
}

